 182.\n\nSo, the final computed product is 182.\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n\n1. **Multiply 13 by 4 (ones place of 14):**\n   - 13 \u00d7 4 = 52\n\n2. **Multiply 13 by 10 (tens place of 14):**\n   - 13 \u00d7 10 = 130\n\n3. **Add the partial products together:**\n   - 52 + 130 = 182\n\n**Final Answer:**\nThe product of 13 and 14 is 182.\n\n---\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 14 and 15?\n\n# Reasoning:\n\nLet's think step by step. 15 has two digits, so we can reason in two steps.\n\n1. Multiply 14 by the ones place digit 5 of 15.\n2. Multiply 14 by the tens place digit 10 of 15.\n\nNow, sum all the step results: 70 + 140 = 210.\n\nSo, the final computed product is 210.\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n\n1. **Multiply 14 by 5 (ones place of 15):**\n   - 14 \u00d7 5 = 70\n\n2. **Multiply 14 by 10 (tens place of 15):**\n   - 14 \u00d7 10 = 140\n\n3. **Add the partial products together:**\n   - 70 + 140 = 210\n\n**Final Answer:**\nThe product of 14 and 15 is 210.\n\n---\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 15 and 16?\n\n# Reasoning:\n\nLet's think step by step. 16 has two digits, so we can reason in two steps.\n\n1. Multiply 15 by the ones place digit 6 of 16.\n2. Multiply 15 by the tens place digit 10 of 16.\n\nNow, sum all the step results: 90 + 150 = 240.\n\nSo, the final computed product is 240.\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n\n1. **Multiply 15 by 6 (ones place of 16):**\n   - 15 \u00d7 6 = 90\n\n2. **Multiply 15 by 10 (tens place of 16):**\n   - 15 \u00d7 10 = 150\n\n3. **Add the partial products together:**\n   - 90 + 150 = 240\n\n**Final Answer:**\nThe product of 15 and 16 is 240.\n\n---\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 16 and 17?\n\n# Reasoning:\n\nLet's think step by step. 17 has two digits, so we can reason in two steps.\n\n1. Multiply 16 by the ones place digit 7 of 17.\n2. Multiply 16 by the tens place digit 10 of 17.\n\nNow, sum all the step results: 112 + 160 = 272.\n\nSo, the final computed product is 272.\n\n**Step-by-Step Explana