, so we can reason in two steps.\n\n1. Multiply 35 by the ones place digit 6 of 36.\n2. Multiply 35 by the tens place digit 30 of 36.\n\nNow, sum all the step results: 210 + 1,050 = 1,260.\n\nSo, the final computed product is 1,260.\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n\n1. **Multiply 35 by 6 (ones place of 36):**\n   - 35 \u00d7 6 = 210\n\n2. **Multiply 35 by 30 (tens place of 36):**\n   - 35 \u00d7 30 = 1,050\n\n3. **Add the partial products together:**\n   - 210 + 1,050 = 1,260\n\n**Final Answer:**\nThe product of 35 and 36 is 1,260.\n\n---\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 36 and 37?\n\n# Reasoning:\n\nLet's think step by step. 37 has two digits, so we can reason in two steps.\n\n1. Multiply 36 by the ones place digit 7 of 37.\n2. Multiply 36 by the tens place digit 30 of 37.\n\nNow, sum all the step results: 252 + 1,080 = 1,332.\n\nSo, the final computed product is 1,332.\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n\n1. **Multiply 36 by 7 (ones place of 37):**\n   - 36 \u00d7 7 = 252\n\n2. **Multiply 36 by 30 (tens place of 37):**\n   - 36 \u00d7 30 = 1,080\n\n3. **Add the partial products together:**\n   - 252 + 1,080 = 1,332\n\n**Final Answer:**\nThe product of 36 and 37 is 1,332.\n\n---\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 37 and 38?\n\n# Reasoning:\n\nLet's think step by step. 38 has two digits, so we can reason in two steps.\n\n1. Multiply 37 by the ones place digit 8 of 38.\n2. Multiply 37 by the tens place digit 30 of 38.\n\nNow, sum all the step results: 296 + 1,110 = 1,406.\n\nSo, the final computed product is 1,406.\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n\n1. **Multiply 37 by 8 (ones place of 38):**\n   - 37 \u00d7 8 = 296\n\n2. **Multiply 37 by 30 (tens place of 38):**\n   - 37 \u00d7 30 = 1,110\n\n3. **Add the partial products together:**\n   - 296 + 1,110 = 1,406\n\n**Final Answer:**\nThe product of 37 and 38 is 1,406.\n\n---\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 38 and 39?\n\n# Reasoning:\n\nLet's think step by step. 39 has two digits, so we can reason in t